# App integration — chat commands & cross-app APIs

Apps do **not** read or write **another app's private** collections (`{otherapp}_*`). Another app (or chat-server) adds data to them by calling the **target app’s HTTP API** with the **user’s JWT** forwarded.

**Exception — Space Core Records** (`core-records.mdc`): shared customers/suppliers (`suite_clients`), items (`suite_items`), and invoices are read by every Space app through ZAPI and written through `/apps/suite/*` (`@vtc/suite-core`). Do not build an HTTP hop to Customers/Invoicing for those.

## Three surfaces

| Surface | Who calls | Pattern |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| **Chat commands** | User in VTC chat | `/appshortname ?` → chat-server → target `POST/GET /api/*` |
| **Server** | Another VTC child app | `fetch` to `{TARGET}_APP_URL` + same JWT query params |
| **Shell chat deeplink** | Child app → platform UI | `{PLATFORM_URL}/dashboard/chat/with/{userId}` — see below |

## Platform chat deep links (child app → network chat)

Child apps link **into the VTC shell** (posif-svelte repo), not `chat.vtc.com`. Chat REST/Socket.IO stays internal to the shell — `realtime.mdc`.

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/dashboard/chat/with/{userId}` | Find or create a DM with that user, then open the room |
| `/dashboard/chat/{roomId}` | Open an existing room by Mongo `_id` |

`userId` is the platform user id — same value as JWT `user_id` / URL param `user`.

**Env:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_URL` — shell origin only (e.g. `https://app.vtc.com`, beta `https://beta.vtc.com`). Never hardcode.

```typescript
const shell = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_URL!.replace(/\/$/, '')
const otherUserId = '29457' // JWT user_id of the person to message
const url = `${shell}/dashboard/chat/with/${encodeURIComponent(otherUserId)}`
```

When the app runs inside the shell iframe, resolve shell origin from `NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_URL`, `document.referrer`, or shell query params (`shell`, `parent`, `return`) — reference: `~/apps/barter/src/lib/platformShell.ts`.

**Helpers (copy or import pattern):**

```typescript
export function getChatWithUserPath(otherUserId: string): string {
  return `/dashboard/chat/with/${encodeURIComponent(otherUserId)}`
}

export function getChatWithUserUrl(otherUserId: string, shellOrigin: string): string {
  return `${shellOrigin.replace(/\/$/, '')}${getChatWithUserPath(otherUserId)}`
}
```

**Shell implementation:** `posif-svelte` → `src/lib/features/chat/open-chat.ts` (`getChatWithUserPath`, `openChatWithUser`), route `src/routes/(authenticated)/dashboard/chat/with/[userId]/+page.svelte`.

**Auth:** User must be logged into the **shell** (`app.vtc.com` / `beta.vtc.com`). Unauthenticated visits redirect to `/login?redirect=…` with the chat path preserved. Child app JWT/localStorage is separate — do not assume opening the shell URL inherits the child app session (`auth-bootstrap.mdc`).

**DM policy:** Creation may be blocked by network DM scope — handle errors in UI; see `posif-svelte/docs/dm-policy-api-spec.md`.

## Canonical server call (app → app)

1. Env: `{TARGET}_APP_URL` (server only). Example: `KANBAN_APP_URL=https://kanban.vtc.com`
2. Build URL with auth query params (required):

```typescript
const base = process.env.KANBAN_APP_URL!.replace(/\/$/, '')
const url = new URL('/api/tasks', `${base}/`)
url.searchParams.set('token', userJwt)
url.searchParams.set('user', user.user_id)
url.searchParams.set('group', user.group_id === '0' ? '0' : user.group_id)
```

3. `POST` JSON body; use standard envelope from `api-routes.mdc`:

```typescript
const res = await fetch(url, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${userJwt}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ boardId, name }),
})
const result = await res.json()
if (!result.success) throw new Error(result.error)
```

4. Implement client in `src/lib/{target}Client.ts` (server-side only). Proxy from your app’s `/api/*` if the browser must not see `{TARGET}_APP_URL`.

**Reference:** `suggestions/src/lib/kanbanClient.ts`, `chat-server/src/services/kanbanClient.ts`

## Kanban — commands & write APIs (today)

**Chat** (private — reply only to sender; register app in chat-server `PRIVATE_COMMAND_APPS`):

```
/kanban ?                          — help
/kanban boards                     — list boards
/kanban link <board>               — default board for add
/kanban add <title>                — task on default board
/kanban add <title> to <board>     — task on named board
```

**HTTP** (any server with user JWT):

| Method | Path | Body / params |
|--------|------|----------------|
| GET | `/api/boards` | — |
| POST | `/api/tasks` | `{ boardId, name, status?, subSteps?, addedBy? }` |

## Suggestions — commands & write APIs

**Chat** (private; `PRIVATE_COMMAND_APPS`):

```
/suggestions ?                              — help
/suggestions add <title>                    — submit idea
/suggestions add <title> — <details>        — with optional body
/suggestions list                           — top open by votes
/suggestions promote <id or title> to <board> — admin → Kanban task
```

**HTTP:**

| Method | Path | Body |
|--------|------|------|
| GET | `/api/suggestions/list` | `filter`, `sort`, `limit` |
| POST | `/api/suggestions/create` | `{ title, body?, source? }` |
| POST | `/api/suggestions/promote` | `{ suggestionId, boardId }` (admin) |

## Adding a new integratable app

1. **Expose** list/create (and other writes) under `src/app/api/` — `api-routes.mdc` layout.
2. **Document** chat subcommands in a `?` help string (`/appshortname ?`).
3. **Chat-server:** `parseSlashCommand` → handler in `commands/{app}Command.ts` → `{app}Client.ts`; add app to `PRIVATE_COMMAND_APPS` if replies must not hit the room.
4. **Consumers:** add `{APP}_APP_URL` to `env_development` + committed `.env.production` / `env_production`.
5. **Client deep links only:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_{APP}_APP_URL` — never put API keys or server-only URLs in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

## Rules

- Never read another app’s private MongoDB collections directly. Core Records (`core-records.mdc`) are shared on purpose — use `@vtc/suite-core`.
- Never hardcode `*.posif.com` — use env (`env-development.mdc`).
- Permissions are enforced by the **target** app from JWT (`role_type`, board access, etc.).
- Browser clients call **same-origin** `/api/*` only; cross-app calls are server-side.

